  "elements": [
    {
      "id": "0L7WAkmUsEsOfUuNlum-T",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 340.7717604658983,
      "y": 106.125,
      "width": 728.8906250000001,
      "height": 1875,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bDp",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1322496347,
      "version": 1882,
      "versionNonce": 949821083,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1742981209574,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Design youtube\n\nFunctional requirements:\n\n1. Users can upload videos\n2. Users can stream/watch videos\n\nScale:\n1M uploads/day\n100M DAU\nMax video size -> 256GB\n\nNon functional requirements:\n\n1. Scalability -> uploads and streams\n2. Availability >> consistency \n3. Eventual consistency\n4. Uploads for large video size\n5. Low latency -> streams (< 500ms)\n6. Different resolutions -> 360p, 480p, ... , 4k\n\nBack of the envelope calculation:\n\n1. Throughput\nuploads: 1M/ 10^5 -> 10 TPS\nstream: 100M * 5 / 10^5 -> 5k TPS -> 5k * 10 -> 50k Minute of content\nper second\n\n2. Storage\n1M * 10 -> 10M minutes \n1080p: 1 hour -> 2GB -> 60 -> 2k MB/60 - 350MB\n\nAssumption: Factor of 3 to get all resolutions\n350 * 3 ~ 1GB * 1 M ~ 1PB\n10 year ~ 3650 * 1PB ~ 3.65 EB\n\nCore entities:\n\n1. Video -> object store\n2. VideoMetadata\nPK -> videoId\nSK -> \"CHUNK#1\"\nsequenceNumber?: 1\nduration\nsizeBytes: number\ntype: VideoType(VIDEO, VIDEO_CHUNK)\nformat: Format (1080, 480, ..)\nstatus: VideoStatus (CHUNKING, COMPLETED, CHUNKING_STARTED)\ncreatedAt: timestamp\ndescription: varchar(500)\nthumbnail: varchar(200)\n\nAPIs:\n\n1. POST /api/v1/video\nRequest body ->\n{\n    Video,\n    VideoMetadata\n}\n\nResponse -> \n{\n    presignedUrl from S3\n}\n\n2. GET /api/v1/video/{videoId}?page=1&limit=10\nResponse ->\n{\n    [{\n        \"chunkId\": \"\",\n        \"presignedUrl from S3\": \"\"\n    }]\n}\n    ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Design youtube\n\nFunctional requirements:\n\n1. Users can upload videos\n2. Users can stream/watch videos\n\nScale:\n1M uploads/day\n100M DAU\nMax video size -> 256GB\n\nNon functional requirements:\n\n1. Scalability -> uploads and streams\n2. Availability >> consistency \n3. Eventual consistency\n4. Uploads for large video size\n5. Low latency -> streams (< 500ms)\n6. Different resolutions -> 360p, 480p, ... , 4k\n\nBack of the envelope calculation:\n\n1. Throughput\nuploads: 1M/ 10^5 -> 10 TPS\nstream: 100M * 5 / 10^5 -> 5k TPS -> 5k * 10 -> 50k Minute of content per second\n\n2. Storage\n1M * 10 -> 10M minutes \n1080p: 1 hour -> 2GB -> 60 -> 2k MB/60 - 350MB\n\nAssumption: Factor of 3 to get all resolutions\n350 * 3 ~ 1GB * 1 M ~ 1PB\n10 year ~ 3650 * 1PB ~ 3.65 EB\n\nCore entities:\n\n1. Video -> object store\n2. VideoMetadata\nPK -> videoId\nSK -> \"CHUNK#1\"\nsequenceNumber?: 1\nduration\nsizeBytes: number\ntype: VideoType(VIDEO, VIDEO_CHUNK)\nformat: Format (1080, 480, ..)\nstatus: VideoStatus (CHUNKING, COMPLETED, CHUNKING_STARTED)\ncreatedAt: timestamp\ndescription: varchar(500)\nthumbnail: varchar(200)\n\nAPIs:\n\n1. POST /api/v1/video\nRequest body ->\n{\n    Video,\n    VideoMetadata\n}\n\nResponse -> \n{\n    presignedUrl from S3\n}\n\n2. GET /api/v1/video/{videoId}?page=1&limit=10\nResponse ->\n{\n    [{\n        \"chunkId\": \"\",\n        \"presignedUrl from S3\": \"\"\n    }]\n}\n    ",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
